31,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems our dear friends in the conservation lab are quite overwhelmed, and our volunteers are mostly tied to the town history circle. I worry we are asking too much of too few.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shion,,"My findings are less heartwarming. We have a recurring failure with lender paperwork missing shipping cut-offs, and our powered displays are prone to frequent, public breakdowns. We are playing a dangerous game with our reliability.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,May,,"And here is the real tea! It turns out our ""prestigious"" static displays are actually bores. People only come back if there's something moving or a friendly face to talk to. Static cases are just where interest goes to die!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The structural survey shows the suspended bay has a strict weight limit. Additionally, evening hire bookings mean the gallery must accommodate caterers and furniture, which has previously led to damage for open displays.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Wow, I found the secret money-eaters! Shipping and insurance are eating up a huge chunk of the budget, and the joiner's rates are going up and up! It's like the money is just disappearing into crates!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Sakura, it does sound like a bit of a puzzle, doesn't it? But I am more concerned that our staff are stretched so thin. We must be very gentle with their workload.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@May, your ""tea"" is a liability. If the public demands movement, but our powered displays are constantly breaking down and being roped off, we are simply inviting public disappointment.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shion, you're such a killjoy! We just need a display that actually works. Why settle for a boring room when we can give the people something they'll actually talk about?","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, if we prioritize movement and crowds, we must consider the physical toll. The gallery is not just a display; it is a working building that hosts evening events. We cannot risk fragile or oversized installations.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Misaki, you're right! If we have big, heavy things, they might break the floor or get bumped by the party people. And @Shion, if the power keeps breaking, maybe we should just avoid the fancy plugs!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Sakura, you have such a wonderful way of simplifying things. If we avoid the fancy plugs and heavy crates, perhaps our tired staff in the lab and the gallery won't feel so burdened.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shion,,"Simplification is a luxury we cannot afford if it means ignoring the pattern of failure. We don't just need to avoid ""fancy plugs""; we need to avoid any project with complex international logistics that will miss its cut-off.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shion, you're treating this like a funeral! Let's be real: a safe, boring show is just a different kind of failure. If the visitors are yawning, we've already lost. We need a spark, just a reliable one!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@May, a spark is useless if the installation is damaged by catering staff or exceeds the weight limit of the suspended bay. We need a proposal that is physically resilient and compact.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@May, a spark is great, but maybe a spark that doesn't cost a mountain of money to ship! If we pick something that already has its own stands, we can save all those coins for something fun!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Shizue,,It is so heartening to see you all thinking of the museum's future. Let us remember that the most beautiful exhibition is one that brings peace to both the visitors and the people working behind the scenes.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Shion,,"Peace is a byproduct of efficiency, Shizue. If we select a project that is logistically sound and mechanically simple, the peace will follow. Let us see which candidates actually survive this scrutiny.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,May,,"I'm with Shion on the efficiency part, but only if it doesn't mean a snooze-fest! Let's find something that's a crowd-pleaser but won't make the staff cry or the floor collapse. I'm ready for the candidates!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I agree. We need a balance between visitor appeal and operational reality. A project that respects the building's limits and the staff's capacity is the only sustainable choice. I am ready to review the proposals.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Sakura,,I'm ready too! I've got my detective hat on and I'm looking for the one that doesn't swallow all our money. Let's see who the lucky winner is!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
52,2,4,pass,Sakura,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
